Dynamo Frontend: HTTP+Pre-processor+Router

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit

Dynamo Frontend Options:
  -i, --interactive, --no-interactive
                        Interactive text chat.
                        env var: DYN_INTERACTIVE
  --namespace NAMESPACE
                        Dynamo namespace for model discovery scoping. Use for exact namespace matching. If --namespace-prefix is also specified, prefix takes precedence.
                        env var: DYN_NAMESPACE | default: None
  --kv-cache-block-size KV_CACHE_BLOCK_SIZE
                        KV cache block size (u32).
                        env var: DYN_KV_CACHE_BLOCK_SIZE | default: None
  --http-host HTTP_HOST
                        HTTP host for the engine (str).
                        env var: DYN_HTTP_HOST | default: 0.0.0.0
  --http-port HTTP_PORT
                        HTTP port for the engine (u16).
                        env var: DYN_HTTP_PORT | default: 8000
  --batch-gateway-url BATCH_GATEWAY_URL
                        Internal Batch Gateway URL for proxying /v1/files and /v1/batches.
                        env var: DYN_BATCH_GATEWAY_URL | default: None
  --serve-indexer, --no-serve-indexer
                        Serve this frontend's local KV indexers over the request plane.
                        env var: DYN_SERVE_INDEXER | default: False
  --tls-cert-path TLS_CERT_PATH
                        TLS certificate path, PEM format.
                        env var: DYN_TLS_CERT_PATH | default: None
  --tls-key-path TLS_KEY_PATH
                        TLS certificate key path, PEM format.
                        env var: DYN_TLS_KEY_PATH | default: None
  --tls-client-ca-cert-path TLS_CLIENT_CA_CERT_PATH
                        Client CA certificate path for mutual TLS, PEM format.
                        env var: DYN_TLS_CLIENT_CA_CERT_PATH | default: None
  --tcp-tls-cert-path TCP_TLS_CERT_PATH
                        Path to PEM certificate for the TCP server.
                        env var: DYN_TCP_TLS_CERT_PATH | default: None
  --tcp-tls-key-path TCP_TLS_KEY_PATH
                        Path to PEM private key for the TCP server certificate.
                        env var: DYN_TCP_TLS_KEY_PATH | default: None
  --tcp-tls-ca-cert-path TCP_TLS_CA_CERT_PATH
                        Path to PEM CA certificate used to verify the TCP peer's certificate.
                        env var: DYN_TCP_TLS_CA_CERT_PATH | default: None
  --tcp-tls-client-cert-path TCP_TLS_CLIENT_CERT_PATH
                        Path to PEM client certificate presented to the TCP server for mTLS.
                        env var: DYN_TCP_TLS_CLIENT_CERT_PATH | default: None
  --tcp-tls-client-key-path TCP_TLS_CLIENT_KEY_PATH
                        Path to PEM private key for the TCP client certificate (mTLS).
                        env var: DYN_TCP_TLS_CLIENT_KEY_PATH | default: None
  --tcp-tls-client-ca-cert-path TCP_TLS_CLIENT_CA_CERT_PATH
                        Path to PEM CA certificate the TCP server uses to verify client certificates. When set, clients must present a trusted certificate (mTLS enforced).
                        env var: DYN_TCP_TLS_CLIENT_CA_CERT_PATH | default: None
  --nats-tls-ca-cert-path NATS_TLS_CA_CERT_PATH
                        Path to PEM CA certificate for verifying the NATS server.
                        env var: NATS_TLS_CA_CERT_PATH | default: None
  --nats-tls-insecure, --no-nats-tls-insecure
                        Disable NATS TLS certificate verification. For local development only.
                        env var: NATS_TLS_INSECURE | default: False
  --nats-tls-client-cert-path NATS_TLS_CLIENT_CERT_PATH
                        Path to PEM client certificate presented to the NATS server for mTLS.
                        env var: NATS_TLS_CLIENT_CERT_PATH | default: None
  --nats-tls-client-key-path NATS_TLS_CLIENT_KEY_PATH
                        Path to PEM private key for the NATS client certificate (mTLS).
                        env var: NATS_TLS_CLIENT_KEY_PATH | default: None
  --namespace-prefix NAMESPACE_PREFIX
                        Dynamo namespace prefix for model discovery scoping. Discovers models from namespaces starting with this prefix (e.g., 'ns' matches 'ns', 'ns-abc123', 'ns-def456'). Takes precedence over --namespace if both are specified.
                        env var: DYN_NAMESPACE_PREFIX | default: None
  --migration-limit MIGRATION_LIMIT
                        Maximum number of times a request may be migrated to a different engine worker. When > 0, enables migration after worker disconnects, response timeouts, incomplete streams, and worker-local overload rejection. Also limits replacement attempts over the lifetime of an explicit-commit PCM realtime transcription session; unfinished audio is replayed to a compatible warm worker.
                        env var: DYN_MIGRATION_LIMIT | default: 0
  --migration-max-seq-len MIGRATION_MAX_SEQ_LEN
                        Maximum sequence length (prompt + generated tokens) for migration state tracking. Once the accumulated token count exceeds this limit, the request becomes non-migratable. Prevents unbounded memory growth from caching long sequences. Default: no limit.
                        env var: DYN_MIGRATION_MAX_SEQ_LEN | default: None
  --model-name MODEL_NAME
                        Model name as a string (e.g., 'Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct')
                        env var: DYN_MODEL_NAME | default: None
  --model-path MODEL_PATH
                        Path to model directory on disk (e.g., /tmp/model_cache/llama3.2_1B/)
                        env var: DYN_MODEL_PATH | default: None
  --metrics-prefix METRICS_PREFIX
                        Prefix for Dynamo frontend metrics. If unset, uses DYN_METRICS_PREFIX env var or 'dynamo_frontend'.
                        env var: DYN_METRICS_PREFIX | default: None
  --kserve-grpc-server, --no-kserve-grpc-server
                        Start KServe gRPC server.
                        env var: DYN_KSERVE_GRPC_SERVER | default: False
  --grpc-metrics-port GRPC_METRICS_PORT
                        HTTP metrics port for gRPC service (u16). Only used with --kserve-grpc-server. Defaults to 8788.
                        env var: DYN_GRPC_METRICS_PORT | default: 8788
  --dump-config-to DUMP_CONFIG_TO
                        Dump config to the specified file path.
                        env var: DYN_DUMP_CONFIG_TO | default: None
  --frontend-route-extension FRONTEND_ROUTE_EXTENSIONS
                        Trusted frontend route extension: a name registered under the 'dynamo.frontend.routes' entry-point group, or a 'module:function' path. May be repeated. DYN_FRONTEND_ROUTE_EXTENSIONS accepts whitespace-separated values.
                        env var: DYN_FRONTEND_ROUTE_EXTENSIONS | default: []
  --discovery-backend {kubernetes,etcd,file,mem}
                        Discovery backend: kubernetes (K8s API), etcd (distributed KV), file (local filesystem), mem (in-memory). Etcd uses the ETCD_* env vars (e.g. ETCD_ENDPOINTS) for connection details. File uses root dir from env var DYN_FILE_KV or defaults to $TMPDIR/dynamo_store_kv.
                        env var: DYN_DISCOVERY_BACKEND | default: etcd
  --request-plane {nats,tcp}
                        Determines how requests are distributed from routers to workers. 'tcp' is fastest [nats|tcp]
                        env var: DYN_REQUEST_PLANE | default: tcp
  --response-plane {tcp,quic,velo}
                        Select the response transport. Frontend and workers must match.
                        env var: DYN_RESPONSE_PLANE | default: tcp
  --event-plane {nats,zmq}
                        Determines how events are published [nats|zmq]. If unset, defaults to 'zmq' for all discovery backends. Set to 'nats' to use a NATS-based event plane.
                        env var: DYN_EVENT_PLANE | default: None
  --enable-anthropic-api, --no-enable-anthropic-api
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] Enable Anthropic Messages API endpoint (/v1/messages). This feature is experimental and may change.
                        env var: DYN_ENABLE_ANTHROPIC_API | default: False
  --enable-systemone-api, --no-enable-systemone-api
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] Enable typed decision APIs (/v1/decisions and /v1/systemone) for qualified aggregate SGLang models.
                        env var: DYN_ENABLE_SYSTEMONE_API | default: False
  --strip-anthropic-preamble, --no-strip-anthropic-preamble
                        Strip the Claude Code billing preamble (x-anthropic-billing-header) from the system prompt. Saves tokens and improves prompt caching.
                        env var: DYN_STRIP_ANTHROPIC_PREAMBLE | default: True
  --reject-media, --no-reject-media
                        Refuse chat requests that carry image, video, or audio content in any message, including history, before routing. For frontends that serve text-only models: a streaming client gets an HTTP error instead of a 200 followed by an error event. The status is set by --reject-media-status-code.
                        env var: DYN_REJECT_MEDIA | default: False
  --reject-media-status-code REJECT_MEDIA_STATUS_CODE
                        HTTP status (4xx or 5xx) for a request refused by --reject-media. Set it to a status an upstream gateway fails over on, such as 429, to send these requests to a multimodal model.
                        env var: DYN_REJECT_MEDIA_STATUS_CODE | default: 415
  --enable-streaming-tool-dispatch, --no-enable-streaming-tool-dispatch
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] Enable streaming tool call dispatch. Emits 'event: tool_call_dispatch' SSE events on /v1/chat/completions for each complete tool call before finish_reason arrives. Can be combined with --enable-streaming-reasoning-dispatch.
                        env var: DYN_ENABLE_STREAMING_TOOL_DISPATCH | default: False
  --enable-streaming-reasoning-dispatch, --no-enable-streaming-reasoning-dispatch
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] Enable streaming reasoning dispatch. Emits a single 'event: reasoning_dispatch' SSE event on /v1/chat/completions with the complete reasoning block once thinking ends. Can be combined with --enable-streaming-tool-dispatch.
                        env var: DYN_ENABLE_STREAMING_REASONING_DISPATCH | default: False
  --reasoning-field-name {reasoning_content,reasoning}
                        OpenAI-compatible response field used for emitted reasoning content.
                        env var: DYN_REASONING_FIELD_NAME | default: reasoning_content
  --exclude-tools-when-tool-choice-none, --no-exclude-tools-when-tool-choice-none
                        Exclude tool definitions from the chat template when tool_choice='none'. Prevents models from generating raw XML tool calls in the content field.
                        env var: DYN_EXCLUDE_TOOLS_WHEN_TOOL_CHOICE_NONE | default: True
  --default-chat-template-kwargs DEFAULT_CHAT_TEMPLATE_KWARGS
                        JSON object of chat template kwargs that apply to every chat request this frontend serves, for every model. Each request's own chat_template_kwargs win per key, except null and "auto" values, and a request thinking control replaces the thinking keys. Set this on the frontend, not on the engine: the frontend renders the chat template, so the engine flag has no effect behind Dynamo.
                        env var: DYN_DEFAULT_CHAT_TEMPLATE_KWARGS | default: None
  --dyn-chat-processor {dynamo,vllm,sglang}
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] Chat pre/post processor backend. 'dynamo' uses the Rust preprocessor. 'vllm' uses local vLLM for pre and post processing. 'sglang' uses SGLang APIs for chat template rendering, tool call parsing, and reasoning parsing.
                        env var: DYN_CHAT_PROCESSOR | default: dynamo
  --dyn-debug-perf, --no-dyn-debug-perf
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] Enable performance instrumentation for diagnosing preprocessing bottlenecks. Logs per-function timing, request concurrency, and hot-path section durations. Supported with '--dyn-chat-processor vllm' and '--dyn-chat-processor sglang'.
                        env var: DYN_DEBUG_PERF | default: False
  --dyn-preprocess-workers PREPROCESS_WORKERS
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] SGLang preprocessing worker processes per model. When unset, selects up to 2 workers per model from visible CPU capacity, leaving one CPU out of the per-model calculation. Multiple models each create a pool. 0 runs preprocessing on the main event loop. Nonzero values are supported only with '--dyn-chat-processor sglang'.
                        env var: DYN_PREPROCESS_WORKERS | default: auto for SGLang, 0 otherwise
  --tokenizer {default,fastokens,basetenkenizer}
                        Tokenizer backend for BPE models: 'default' (HuggingFace tokenizers library), 'fastokens' (fastokens crate for high-performance BPE encoding), or 'basetenkenizer' (Baseten Tokenizer for native encoding and decoding). Has no effect on TikToken models.
                        env var: DYN_TOKENIZER | default: default
  --tokenizer-fallback, --no-tokenizer-fallback
                        Automatic fallback to HuggingFace is deprecated and will be disabled by default in a future release. The current behavior falls back when the selected fastokens or basetenkenizer backend cannot load the model tokenizer. Use --no-tokenizer-fallback to fail model initialization instead. In dynamic mode, discovery retries the load while the frontend continues running.
                        env var: DYN_TOKENIZER_FALLBACK | default: True
  --trust-remote-code, --no-trust-remote-code
                        Trust remote code when loading the tokenizer. Required for models that ship custom tokenizer code (e.g. Qwen, Falcon).
                        env var: DYN_TRUST_REMOTE_CODE | default: False

Router Options:
  --enforce-disagg, --no-enforce-disagg
                        DEPRECATED: accepted for compatibility but ignored. Routing topology and readiness are determined from registered worker types.
                        env var: DYN_ENFORCE_DISAGG | default: False
  --router-min-initial-workers MIN_INITIAL_WORKERS
                        Minimum number of workers required before router startup continues. This is exported as DYN_ROUTER_MIN_INITIAL_WORKERS so the generic push-router path and the KV router's config-ready worker gate share the same startup threshold. Set to 0 to disable the startup wait.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_MIN_INITIAL_WORKERS | default: 0
  --router-mode {round-robin,random,kv,direct,least-loaded,device-aware-weighted}
                        How to route the request. least-loaded routes to the worker with the fewest active requests. device-aware-weighted routes based on worker device type (CPU/CUDA). In disaggregated prefill mode, least-loaded skips bootstrap optimization and falls back to the synchronous prefill path.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_MODE | default: round-robin
  --router-session-affinity-ttl-secs SESSION_AFFINITY_TTL_SECS
                        Enable session affinity with this router-local idle TTL in seconds. Bindings synchronize across router replicas on a best-effort basis. Affinity is disabled when this option is omitted. This is independent of KV prediction TTL settings.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_SESSION_AFFINITY_TTL_SECS | default: None
  --router-session-affinity-max-entries SESSION_AFFINITY_MAX_ENTRIES
                        Most sessions each session-affinity table holds at once; the frontend keeps one table per worker set. A request that would start a new session past this limit is rejected as resource exhausted (HTTP 529 by default) until an idle session expires. Replica sync copies bindings to every frontend, so size it for the sessions live across all frontends. Has no effect unless --router-session-affinity-ttl-secs is set. This is exported as DYN_ROUTER_SESSION_AFFINITY_MAX_ENTRIES, where every affinity table reads it.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_SESSION_AFFINITY_MAX_ENTRIES | default: 65536
  --router-session-affinity-mode {hard,soft}
                        How an existing session binding participates in worker selection. hard makes the binding an exact constraint; soft exposes it as a policy-visible preference.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_SESSION_AFFINITY_MODE | default: hard
  --active-decode-blocks-threshold ACTIVE_DECODE_BLOCKS_THRESHOLD
                        Threshold fraction (0.0-1.0) of KV cache block utilization above which a worker is considered busy. Setting a numeric value enables this rejection check. Unset by default; pass 'None' to disable it.
                        env var: DYN_ACTIVE_DECODE_BLOCKS_THRESHOLD | default: None
  --active-prefill-tokens-threshold ACTIVE_PREFILL_TOKENS_THRESHOLD
                        Deprecated; will be removed in v1.7. Use --active-prefill-tokens-threshold-frac. Literal token count threshold for determining when a worker is considered busy based on prefill token utilization. When active prefill tokens exceed this threshold, the worker is marked as busy. Setting a numeric value enables this rejection check. Unset by default; pass 'None' to disable it. Uses OR logic with --active-prefill-tokens-threshold-frac.
                        env var: DYN_ACTIVE_PREFILL_TOKENS_THRESHOLD | default: None
  --active-prefill-tokens-threshold-frac ACTIVE_PREFILL_TOKENS_THRESHOLD_FRAC
                        Fraction of max_num_batched_tokens for busy detection. Worker is busy when active_prefill_tokens > frac * max_num_batched_tokens. Setting a numeric value enables this rejection check. Unset by default; pass 'None' to disable it. Uses OR logic with --active-prefill-tokens-threshold.
                        env var: DYN_ACTIVE_PREFILL_TOKENS_THRESHOLD_FRAC | default: None

KV Router Options:
  --load-aware, --no-load-aware
                        --load-aware is deprecated and will be removed in v1.7; use the load-only policy and router tracking settings in --router-policy-config. KV Router: Enable the load-aware routing preset. On the frontend, this implies --router-mode kv. This preset sets overlap_score_credit=0, disables KV events and KV-reuse assumptions, enables active-block and prefill-token load tracking, and disables remote/shared cache indexers. The builtin policy does not request cache inputs in this mode.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_LOAD_AWARE | default: False
  --router-kv-overlap-score-credit OVERLAP_SCORE_CREDIT
                        --router-kv-overlap-score-credit is deprecated and will be removed in v1.7; use overlap_score_credit in the default policy parameters in --router-policy-config. KV Router: Credit multiplier for device-local prefix overlap. Must be finite and non-negative; values above 1.0 give device overlap extra credit, with adjusted prefill cost clamped at zero.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_KV_OVERLAP_SCORE_CREDIT | default: 1.0
  --router-kv-overlap-score-credit-decay OVERLAP_SCORE_CREDIT_DECAY
                        --router-kv-overlap-score-credit-decay is deprecated and will be removed in v1.7; use overlap_score_credit_decay in the default policy parameters in --router-policy-config. KV Router: Decay rate for device-local overlap credit as active prefill load rises above the least-loaded eligible worker. 0 disables decay; 1 halves credit at one request-equivalent of excess active prefill load.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_KV_OVERLAP_SCORE_CREDIT_DECAY | default: 0.0
  --router-prefill-load-scale PREFILL_LOAD_SCALE
                        --router-prefill-load-scale is deprecated and will be removed in v1.7; use prefill_load_scale in the default policy parameters in --router-policy-config. KV Router: Scale applied to adjusted prompt-side prefill load after overlap and lower-tier cache-hit credits are subtracted.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_PREFILL_LOAD_SCALE | default: 1.0
  --router-decode-active-request-weight DECODE_ACTIVE_REQUEST_WEIGHT
                        --router-decode-active-request-weight is deprecated and will be removed in v1.7; use decode_active_request_weight in the default policy parameters in --router-policy-config. [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Block-equivalent decode cost added for each active request on a candidate worker. Use this to balance decode batch size when step latency depends more on request count than resident KV footprint. Must be finite and non-negative.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_DECODE_ACTIVE_REQUEST_WEIGHT | default: 0.0
  --router-host-cache-hit-weight HOST_CACHE_HIT_WEIGHT
                        KV Router: Credit multiplier for host-pinned (CPU offload) prefix overlap. Range: 0.0 to 1.0; higher values more strongly prefer workers holding the prefix in CPU-tier KV cache. Symmetric to --router-kv-overlap-score-credit but applied to host_pinned tier overlap.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_HOST_CACHE_HIT_WEIGHT | default: 0.75
  --router-disk-cache-hit-weight DISK_CACHE_HIT_WEIGHT
                        KV Router: Credit multiplier for disk/lower-tier (e.g. NVMe-backed) prefix overlap. Range: 0.0 to 1.0. Same semantics as --router-host-cache-hit-weight applied to the disk tier.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_DISK_CACHE_HIT_WEIGHT | default: 0.25
  --router-temperature ROUTER_TEMPERATURE
                        --router-temperature is deprecated and will be removed in v1.7; use router_temperature in the default policy parameters in --router-policy-config. KV Router: Temperature for normalized worker sampling via softmax. Higher values promote more randomness, and 0 falls back to deterministic.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_TEMPERATURE | default: 0.0
  --router-kv-events, --no-router-kv-events, --kv-events, --no-kv-events
                        KV Router: Enable/disable KV events. Use --router-kv-events to enable (default, router receives cache state events from workers) or --no-router-kv-events to disable (router predicts cache state based on routing decisions).
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_USE_KV_EVENTS | default: True
                        deprecating flag: --kv-events
  --router-replica-sync, --no-router-replica-sync
                        KV Router: Enable best-effort active-sequence synchronization through the Runtime event plane.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_REPLICA_SYNC | default: False
  --router-track-active-blocks, --no-router-track-active-blocks, --track-active-blocks, --no-track-active-blocks
                        KV Router: Track active blocks (blocks being used for ongoing generation). By default, active blocks are tracked for load balancing.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_TRACK_ACTIVE_BLOCKS | default: True
                        deprecating flag: --track-active-blocks
  --router-track-output-blocks, --no-router-track-output-blocks, --track-output-blocks, --no-track-output-blocks
                        KV Router: Track output blocks during generation. When enabled, the router adds placeholder blocks as tokens are generated. With expected output sequence length, fractional decay applies to output blocks and the structurally exclusive prompt suffix; shared prompt blocks retain full weight.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_TRACK_OUTPUT_BLOCKS | default: False
                        deprecating flag: --track-output-blocks
  --router-assume-kv-reuse, --no-router-assume-kv-reuse, --assume-kv-reuse, --no-assume-kv-reuse
                        KV Router: When tracking active blocks, assume KV cache reuse. Use --no-router-assume-kv-reuse to generate random hashes instead (when KV cache reuse is not expected).
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_ASSUME_KV_REUSE | default: True
                        deprecating flag: --assume-kv-reuse
  --router-track-prefill-tokens, --no-router-track-prefill-tokens
                        KV Router: Include prompt-side prefill tokens in active load accounting. Use --no-router-track-prefill-tokens to ignore prompt tokens in router prefill-token load, queue pressure, and active_prefill_tokens metrics.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_TRACK_PREFILL_TOKENS | default: True
  --router-tracking-hash {public-xxh3-v1,keyed-xxh3-v1}
                        KV Router: Hash function for router-derived active-sequence identities.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_TRACKING_HASH | default: public-xxh3-v1
  --router-tracking-key-file ROUTER_TRACKING_KEY_FILE
                        KV Router: File containing the 32-byte provider tracking key.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_TRACKING_KEY_FILE | default: None
  --router-tracking-key-id ROUTER_TRACKING_KEY_ID
                        KV Router: Provider-managed tracking-key epoch identifier.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_TRACKING_KEY_ID | default: None
  --router-prefill-load-model {none,ais}
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Prompt-side prefill load model. 'none' keeps static prompt load accounting. 'ais' decays the oldest active prefill request using AISimulate-predicted duration.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_PREFILL_LOAD_MODEL | default: none
  --router-ttl-secs ROUTER_TTL_SECS
                        KV Router: Time-to-live in seconds for blocks when KV events are disabled. Only used when --no-router-kv-events is set.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_TTL_SECS | default: 120.0
  --router-approximate-cache-policy {ttl,lru}
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Retention policy for the local primary approximate indexer used with --no-router-kv-events. 'ttl' keeps the existing time-based behavior; 'lru' uses each worker rank's advertised KV capacity. Side indexers remain TTL-only.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_APPROXIMATE_CACHE_POLICY | default: ttl
  --router-queue-threshold ROUTER_QUEUE_THRESHOLD
                        --router-queue-threshold is deprecated and will be removed in v1.7; use policy_classes[].prefill_busy_threshold_frac in --router-policy-config. KV Router: Queue threshold fraction for prefill token capacity. Requests are queued if all workers exceed this fraction of max_num_batched_tokens. Must be >= 0. Use 0.0 for maximum queueing sensitivity (queue once every eligible worker has active prefill load). Unset by default; setting a numeric value enables router queueing. Note (SGLang backend): when --max-prefill-tokens is not set, MDC's max_num_batched_tokens falls back to max_total_num_tokens (the KV cache pool size), not the per-step prefill window, which inflates the threshold's effective denominator. Set --max-prefill-tokens explicitly for predictable semantics, or use a smaller threshold.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_QUEUE_THRESHOLD | default: None
  --router-policy-config ROUTER_POLICY_CONFIG
                        KV Router: Startup-only YAML configuration for shared router settings, policy-class queues, and per-role worker-selection policies. When omitted, router_queue_threshold and router_queue_policy define one synthetic policy class; queueing remains disabled unless router_queue_threshold is set.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_POLICY_CONFIG | default: None
  --router-conditional-disagg, --no-router-conditional-disagg
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Enable conditional disaggregation. When enabled, the router may bypass the remote prefill step and route requests directly to a decode worker. The configured policy determines whether local prefill and decode is preferable for each request.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_CONDITIONAL_DISAGG | default: False
  --router-conditional-disagg-config JSON
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: JSON object for conditional disaggregation policy settings. Supported fields: policy, eff_isl_threshold, eff_isl_ratio_threshold, prefill_busy_threshold, decode_busy_threshold.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_CONDITIONAL_DISAGG_CONFIG | default: None
  --router-prefill-policy ROUTER_PREFILL_POLICY
                        --router-prefill-policy is deprecated and will be removed in v1.7; use worker_selection.prefill in --router-policy-config. KV Router: Process-local worker-selection policy type for disaggregated prefill workers in this router process. Overrides worker_selection.prefill from --router-policy-config. Use 'default' for Dynamo's built-in worker selector.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_PREFILL_POLICY | default: None
  --router-decode-policy ROUTER_DECODE_POLICY
                        --router-decode-policy is deprecated and will be removed in v1.7; use worker_selection.decode in --router-policy-config. KV Router: Process-local worker-selection policy type for decode workers in this router process. Overrides worker_selection.decode from --router-policy-config. Use 'default' for Dynamo's built-in worker selector.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_DECODE_POLICY | default: None
  --router-event-threads ROUTER_EVENT_THREADS
                        KV Router: Number of KV indexer worker threads. When > 1, uses a concurrent radix tree with a thread pool for higher throughput, including approximate routing when --no-router-kv-events is set.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_EVENT_THREADS | default: 4
  --router-queue-policy {fcfs,wspt}
                        --router-queue-policy is deprecated and will be removed in v1.7; use policy_classes[].queue_policy in --router-policy-config. KV Router: Scheduling policy for the router queue. 'fcfs' (default): first-come first-served with priority bumps — optimizes tail TTFT. 'wspt': weighted shortest processing time (Smith's rule) — optimizes average TTFT.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_QUEUE_POLICY | default: fcfs
  --use-remote-indexer, --no-use-remote-indexer
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Query a remote KV indexer served from the worker component via the request plane instead of maintaining a local radix tree.
                        env var: DYN_USE_REMOTE_INDEXER | default: False
  --enable-session-prefix-index, --no-enable-session-prefix-index
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Track per-session block lineage in a logical prefix index that outlives engine cache eviction. Nothing consumes the index for routing decisions yet.
                        env var: DYN_ENABLE_SESSION_PREFIX_INDEX | default: False
  --shared-cache-multiplier SHARED_CACHE_MULTIPLIER
                        --shared-cache-multiplier is deprecated and will be removed in v1.7; use shared_cache_multiplier in the default policy parameters in --router-policy-config. [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Multiplier for shared cache hits (0.0-1.0). Blocks in the shared cache are less valuable than device-local blocks. E.g. 0.5 means each shared hit counts as half a device-local hit. Also credits blocks a worker can fetch from a peer through a KV fetch hint. The default policy uses 0.5 when shared cache is enabled.
                        env var: DYN_SHARED_CACHE_MULTIPLIER | default: None
  --shared-cache-type {none,hicache}
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Type of external shared KV cache to query. 'none' (default): disabled. 'hicache': query Mooncake master directly for SGLang L3 (HiCache) state using SGLang-compatible Mooncake key derivation.
                        env var: DYN_SHARED_CACHE_TYPE | default: none
  --router-predicted-ttl-secs ROUTER_PREDICTED_TTL_SECS
                        KV Router: Enable predict-on-route with this TTL in seconds for entries in the local side indexer. Requires KV events; omit to disable. Independent of --router-ttl-secs, which covers pure approximate mode.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_PREDICTED_TTL_SECS | default: None

AISimulate Perf Model Options:
  --ais-perf-config AIS_PERF_CONFIG
                        Complete ForwardPassPerfModelConfig as JSON or a JSON/YAML path.
  --ais-backend AIS_BACKEND, --aic-backend AIS_BACKEND
                        AISimulate backend; DYN_AIS_BACKEND. Legacy aic spelling accepted.
  --ais-system AIS_SYSTEM, --aic-system AIS_SYSTEM
                        AISimulate system; DYN_AIS_SYSTEM. Legacy aic spelling accepted.
  --ais-backend-version AIS_BACKEND_VERSION, --aic-backend-version AIS_BACKEND_VERSION
                        AISimulate backend-version; DYN_AIS_BACKEND_VERSION. Legacy aic spelling accepted.
  --ais-tp-size AIS_TP_SIZE, --aic-tp-size AIS_TP_SIZE
                        AISimulate tp-size; DYN_AIS_TP_SIZE. Legacy aic spelling accepted.
  --ais-model-path AIS_MODEL_PATH, --aic-model-path AIS_MODEL_PATH
                        AISimulate model-path; DYN_AIS_MODEL_PATH. Legacy aic spelling accepted.
  --ais-moe-tp-size AIS_MOE_TP_SIZE, --aic-moe-tp-size AIS_MOE_TP_SIZE
                        AISimulate moe-tp-size; DYN_AIS_MOE_TP_SIZE. Legacy aic spelling accepted.
  --ais-moe-ep-size AIS_MOE_EP_SIZE, --aic-moe-ep-size AIS_MOE_EP_SIZE
                        AISimulate moe-ep-size; DYN_AIS_MOE_EP_SIZE. Legacy aic spelling accepted.
  --ais-attention-dp-size AIS_ATTENTION_DP_SIZE, --aic-attention-dp-size AIS_ATTENTION_DP_SIZE
                        AISimulate attention-dp-size; DYN_AIS_ATTENTION_DP_SIZE. Legacy aic spelling accepted.
  --ais-nextn AIS_NEXTN, --aic-nextn AIS_NEXTN
                        AISimulate nextn; DYN_AIS_NEXTN. Legacy aic spelling accepted.
  --ais-nextn-accept-rates AIS_NEXTN_ACCEPT_RATES, --aic-nextn-accept-rates AIS_NEXTN_ACCEPT_RATES
                        Comma-separated conditional acceptance rates: entry i is P(draft i accepted | all earlier drafts were accepted).
  --ais-mtp-seed AIS_MTP_SEED, --aic-mtp-seed AIS_MTP_SEED
                        AISimulate mtp-seed; DYN_AIS_MTP_SEED. Legacy aic spelling accepted.
